# ERP Feature Gap Analysis — Instructions and Checklist

## Purpose

You are analyzing an ERP codebase written in Python. Compare it against the
feature checklist below, which is benchmarked on four leading ERPs:
Odoo, ERPNext, Oracle NetSuite and Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central.
Goal: produce a precise, evidence-based gap analysis that the team can turn
into a build roadmap.

## How to evaluate

1. Inspect the codebase thoroughly before answering: data models/schemas,
   business logic/services, API routes, UI views/screens, background jobs,
   configuration, tests and docs.
2. For EVERY checklist item assign exactly one status:
   - HAVE     — fully usable end-to-end (data model + business logic + UI or API)
   - PARTIAL  — some of it exists (e.g. model only, no workflow/UI; or a basic
                version missing key sub-features listed in the item)
   - MISSING  — nothing relevant exists
   - N/A      — intentionally out of scope for this product (only if the
                codebase/docs make that explicit)
3. Rules:
   - Never mark HAVE from a file or class name alone; find the actual logic.
   - For PARTIAL, state concretely what is missing.
   - Cite evidence as file paths (and function/class names where useful).
   - If you cannot find something after a real search, say MISSING, not "unclear".
4. Tiers (already assigned, do not change them):
   - Core — present in all four benchmark ERPs; customers assume it exists
   - Adv  — present in two or three; what mid-market buyers compare on
   - Edge — present in one vendor or shipped in the last ~18 months;
            differentiation opportunities

## Required output format

### A. Summary by section
A table: Section | Items | HAVE | PARTIAL | MISSING | N/A | Core coverage %

### B. Full results
A table with one row per checklist item:
ID | Feature | Tier | Status | Evidence (paths) | Gap notes

### C. Prioritized gap list
Ordered as: (1) Core MISSING, (2) Core PARTIAL, (3) Adv MISSING,
(4) Adv PARTIAL, (5) Edge. Group by section. For each gap give:
- what to build (one or two sentences)
- dependencies on other items (by ID)
- effort estimate: S (< 1 week), M (1–4 weeks), L (> 1 month) for one developer

### D. Architectural observations
Anything in the codebase that will block Core features at scale (e.g. no
multi-company field on records, no audit trail mechanism, no permission layer,
hard-coded currency or tax logic, no localization framework).

